+   sides of a window (fntClipX0..fntClipX1, display pixels; equal: no window), a glyph that crosses its edge drawn
+   in part. The marquee (fntRenderStringFit) slides its text through that window a display pixel at a time, every
+   frame, where it used to jump a whole character every 200 ms; the description roll places each line to the
+   display pixel instead of the unit. Set by the caller around one string and cleared after it. */
+static float fntSubX = 0.0f, fntSubY = 0.0f;
+static int fntClipX0 = 0, fntClipX1 = 0;
